# Professional Report Standards

## Goal

Produce client-ready KP reports that feel like a senior astrologer’s written deliverable — not a generic LLM dump.

## Required sections (personal)

1. Cover / birth metadata (name, DOB, TOB, place, ayanamsa, coords)
2. Chart synopsis (Lagna, Moon, key CSLs)
3. Persona & life themes
4. Career & vocation (with timing)
5. Relationships & marriage themes (with timing)
6. Finance & gains (non-advisory)
7. Current & upcoming dasha windows
8. Practical guidance (3–7 actions)
9. Optional: significator table appendix, chart image

## Quality bar

- Every major claim cites chart evidence (planet/house/sublord/dasha).
- Timing uses MD/AD (and pratyantar when relevant), not vague “soon”.
- Consistent voice: calm, specific, non-fatalistic.
- Fixed section order and headings across clients.
- PDF: readable typography, tables that don’t overflow, optional AI block never blocks PDF on API failure (match existing `_ai_pdf_summary` behavior).

## Organisation reports

- Foundation chart first; match/overlay second when provided.
- Separate “structural significations” from “forecast windows”.
- Keep org tone institutional, not personal-romance language.
